@michaljelonek I feel that our current docs (and the updated ones) explain what each function does. This information fits better as docstrings in code as those can be updated when the implementation changes. I'd like to see a higher-level explanation of how everything fits together that only mentions the function names and maybe contains a flowchart or two.

Here's an example: https://help.shopify.com/en/api/guides/sell-through-the-checkout-api

If anyone needs to include graphs in docs, I recommend using [Camunda](https://camunda.com/bpmn/tool/) and including both the source BPMN file and the exported graphic.

